    <item>
      <title>Leading Through Change: The Economy, Opportunity and the Future of Work  at Ira Aldridge Theatre</title>
      <description><![CDATA[<div>  <img src="https://localist-images.azureedge.net/photos/54194896649345/huge/dfa5193fd19cc88208bda4ccf7cdbb4adc4a51fb.jpg" style="width: 100%;" />  <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;"><strong>Tue, 13 Oct 2026</strong></div>  <div><p>An engaging, student-centered fireside chat exploring the economic, technological, and leadership forces shaping the world today—and the future of work. The conversation will examine how students can prepare to lead, build wealth, create opportunity, and make an impact in a rapidly changing economy. Speakers will share perspectives on the economy and labor market, business leadership and investment, entrepreneurship, access to capital, workforce trends, and the skills and experiences needed to navigate a successful career. The discussion will also connect these issues to the Howard experience, higher education, student preparation, leadership, and Howard’s mission of developing leaders who create meaningful change.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Moderator</p>

<p>Wayne A. I. Frederick, M.D., MBA, Interim President &amp; President Emeritus, Howard University </p>

<p>Participants</p>

<p>Tom Barkin, President &amp; CEO, Federal Reserve Bank of RichmondLeslie D. Hale, Chair, Howard University Board of Trustees </p>

<p>This conversation will bring together perspectives from economics, business, finance, higher education, and leadership to help Howard students understand the opportunities and challenges ahead—and consider how they can position themselves to lead and shape the future.</p>

<p><a href="https://events.howard.edu/event/leading-through-change-the-economy-opportunity-and-the-future-of-work">View on site</a> | <a href="mailto:?subject=I found an interesting event%3A Leading Through Change%3A The Economy%2C Opportunity and the Future of Work &amp;body=I found an interesting event you may like%3A%0A%0A%0ADate%3A Oct 13%2C 2026%0A%0ADescription%3A%0AAn engaging%2C student-centered fireside chat exploring the economic%2C technological%2C and leadership forces shaping the world today%E2%80%94and the future of work. The conversation will examine how students can prepare to lead%2C build wealth%2C create opportunity%2C and make an impact in a rapidly changing economy. Speakers will share perspectives on the economy and labor market%2C business leadership and investment%2C entrepreneurship%2C access to capital%2C workforce trends%2C and the skills and experiences needed to navigate a successful career. The discussion will also connect these issues to the Howard experience%2C higher education%2C student preparation%2C leadership%2C and Howard%E2%80%99s mission of developing leaders who create meaningful change.%0A%0A %0A%0AModerator%0A%0AWayne A. I. Frederick%2C M.D.%2C MBA%2C Interim President %26 President Emeritus%2C Howard University %0A%0AParticipants%0A%0ATom Barkin%2C President %26 CEO%2C Federal Reserve Bank of RichmondLeslie D. Hale%2C Chair%2C Howard University Board of Trustees %0A%0AThis conversation will bring together perspectives from economics%2C business%2C finance%2C higher education%2C and leadership to help Howard students understand the opportunities and challenges ahead%E2%80%94and consider how they can position themselves to lead and shape the future.%0A%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fevents.howard.edu%2Fevent%2Fleading-through-change-the-economy-opportunity-and-the-future-of-work%0A">Email this event</a></p></div></div>]]></description>
