      <title>Fireside Chat on the Profession of Social Work at Lindsay Hall (Inabel Burns Lindsay Hall - School of Social Work)</title>
      <description><![CDATA[<div>  <img src="https://localist-images.azureedge.net/photos/54195914326215/huge/e718355a271f713b94af2ba11e6c8035a07d1bee.jpg" style="width: 100%;" />  <div style="font-size: 0.9em; color: #555;"><strong>Tue, 13 Oct 2026</strong></div>  <div><p>Join the School of Social Work during Homecoming Week for a Fireside Chat on the Profession of Social Work.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Hear from two national leaders, Anthony Estreet, Ph.D., MBA, LCSW-C, CEO of the National Association of Social Workers, and Halaevalu F. Ofahengaue Vakalahi, PhD, MSW, President and CEO of the Council on Social Work Education, in conversation with HUSSW Dean Sheara Jennings, PhD, MSW.</p>

<p>The discussion will explore pressing issues shaping social work education, licensure, workforce development, and the future of the profession.</p>

<p> </p>

<p>Tuesday, October 13 | 5:30–7:00 p.m.Inabel Burns Lindsay Hall Auditorium | Howard University </p>

<p>Open to students, faculty, alumni, practitioners, community partners, and the public.</p>

